# Per-run output: JMeter results, resource samples, reports.
#
# The directory itself is kept, so a fresh clone shows where runs land. Only its
# contents are ignored.
results/*
!results/.gitkeep

# Generated payloads. NOT committed: the publish set is about 130 MB at 100,000
# resources, and this repository is public.
#
# Build them before a run, which takes about twenty seconds:
#
#     make data
#
# They are deterministic — same config, same metadata, same bytes — so keeping
# them out of git costs nothing but disk. What is committed instead is
# data/CHECKSUMS, a digest of every generated file.
#
#     make verify-data
#
# regenerates and compares against it, failing if anything moved. That is the
# guarantee a committed payload gave, at a few kilobytes.
data/publish-payload/
data/discover-payload/
data/select-payload/

# NOT ignored, deliberately: data/mandiPrice-metadata/ and data/CHECKSUMS.
#
# The metadata is the INPUT — real market, district, state and commodity data
# from Agmarknet, about a megabyte. Fetching it needs credentials and an
# endpoint that is not public, so committing it is what lets someone else
# generate the same payloads and get the same bytes.

# A working checklist, not documentation. It tracks what is left to do on the
# machine it lives on, which is nobody else's business in a public repository --
# what a reader needs is in README.md.
